; Entity handler: head of the Pestilent Beast (room 10)
;
; The yellow dragon head of "Pestilent Beast" (room 10, 4 cells wide, 20 units high): handler of room object kind 14
; (#R$B028, behaviour block #R$957B). The body of the dragon is part of the room's tiles; the head is this sprite, which
; stays where it is and lowers by 2 units (4 pixels) for the last 40 frames of every 110 frames, the time in which the
; Beast breathes fire (#R$B8C5). It is only drawn: there is no hit box test (the three words +$A, +$C and +$E are popped
; and dropped).
; .
; Slot (the layout of the room enemies made by #R$89ED): +2 and +4 not used, +6 word x and +8 word y (8.8, high bytes in
; 2-pixel units), +$A word, +$C word hit box offset and +$E word hit box far corner: not used here, +$10 pointer to the sprite
; block (#R$9580: attribute, height, width, one frame), +$12 byte counter (110 down to 1) and +$13 its reload ($6E),
; +$14 byte the dip (0 or 1; the slot's frame number, but there is only one frame) and +$15 number of frames.
; .
; When the counter equals BEAST_HEAD_DIP (40) the dip becomes 1; when it reaches 0 it is reloaded and the dip becomes
; 0. The draw command's y is the slot's y plus twice the dip, its graphics the one frame of the block (the frame number
; used for the table lookup is forced to 0). The routine goes on to #R$B3D8, which queues it.
;
; SP Slot address + 2 (the handler word was popped by the RET that entered the routine)
@label=UpdateBeastHead
c$B880 POP BC        ; +2, not used
 $B881 POP BC        ; +4, not used
 $B882 POP HL        ; x word
 $B883 LD D,H        ; D = x
 $B884 POP HL        ; y word
 $B885 LD E,H        ; E = y
 $B886 LD H,D        ;
 $B887 LD L,E        ; HL = x (H) and y (L)
 $B888 LD ($5DFE),HL ; SPAWN_POSITION (not used by the head)
 $B88B SRA H         ; x / 4 = byte column
 $B88D SRA H         ;
 $B88F LD ($ACD3),HL ; position of the draw command: y, byte column
 $B892 POP AF        ; +$A, dropped
 $B893 POP AF        ; +$C, dropped
 $B894 POP AF        ; +$E, dropped
 $B895 POP HL        ; sprite block
 $B896 LD A,(HL)     ; attribute
 $B897 INC HL        ;
 $B898 LD ($ACDA),A  ; of the draw command
 $B89B POP BC        ; C counter, B reload
 $B89C POP DE        ; E dip, D number of frames
 $B89D LD A,C        ;
@isub=CP BEAST_HEAD_DIP
 $B89E CP $28        ; 40 frames before the end: lower the head
 $B8A0 JR NZ,$B8A3   ;
 $B8A2 INC E         ;
*$B8A3 DEC C         ; count down
 $B8A4 JR NZ,$B8A9   ;
 $B8A6 LD C,B        ; reload
 $B8A7 LD E,$00      ; raise the head
*$B8A9 PUSH DE       ; store the dip
 $B8AA PUSH BC       ; store the counter
 $B8AB LD A,E        ;
 $B8AC ADD A,A       ; 2 units per step
 $B8AD EXX           ;
 $B8AE LD HL,($ACD3) ; position of the draw command
 $B8B1 ADD A,L       ;
 $B8B2 LD L,A        ; y lower by 2 * dip
 $B8B3 LD ($ACD3),HL ;
 $B8B6 EXX           ;
 $B8B7 XOR A         ;
 $B8B8 LD E,A        ; frame 0 for the table lookup
 $B8B9 EX AF,AF'     ; A' = 0: column offset
 $B8BA LD B,(HL)     ; height
 $B8BB INC HL        ;
 $B8BC LD C,(HL)     ; width
 $B8BD INC HL        ; HL = frame table
 $B8BE LD ($ACD7),BC ; width, height of the draw command
 $B8C2 JP $B3D8      ; graphics = table[0]; queue it
